# UI / tablet

- Thin client: face, chat, reminder list/buttons. Heavy logic stays on the local brain (PC/NUC/Pi).
- Audience: mainly older adults — large text, high contrast, few steps, obvious buttons.
- First viewport: calm companion feel; avoid dashboard clutter.
- Show reminders clearly (due / confirm / snooze). Never hide critical alerts behind chat-only UX.
- Works on older tablets/browsers when possible; avoid heavy frameworks unless justified.
- Offline-friendly UI for essentials; do not require cloud assets for core flows.
- Prefer local/system fonts over CDN font loading for the MVP UI.
- Launch via `py -m ric ui` (stdlib server in `ric/web_server.py`, assets in `ric/web/`).
- No medical diagnosis UI. Labels like “lembrete” / “registo”, not “tratamento prescrito”.
